A bidder may seek an Administrative Review for any omission or breach by the PDE in accordance with the Public Procurement and Disposal of Assets Act, Cap 205, Regulations or Guidelines made thereunder.
The PDE shall promptly provide a bidder who seeks administrative review with:
A summary of the evaluation process;
A comparison of the tenders, proposals, or quotations, including the evaluation criteria used;
The reasons for rejecting the concerned bids; and
The details of the applicable administrative review fees and the account to which the fees are to be paid.
